[16.049724, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[16.051529, "o", "     1\t# How we compute daily ET0\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tThis is the method the `et0` package must follow. It is the daily FAO-56 Penman-Monteith procedure: FAO Irrigation\r\n     4\tand Drainage Paper No. 56, *Crop evapotranspiration* (Allen, Pereira, Raes and Smith, 1998), chapters 3 and 4.\r\n     5\tEquation numbers below are the book's, so you can look any step up there. You do not need the book: everything the\r\n     6\tpipeline needs is on this page.\r\n     7"]
[16.051581, "o", "\t\r\n     8\tET0 is the water a well-watered reference grass surface would lose in one day, in mm/day. We publish one value per\r\n     9\tstation per day.\r\n    10\t\r\n    11\t## 1. Inputs, after conversion to standard form\r\n    12\t\r\n    13\t| Symbol | Meaning | Unit |\r\n    14\t|---|---|---|\r\n    15\t| Tmax, Tmin | daily maximum and minimum air temperature | deg C |\r\n    16"]
[16.051609, "o", "\t| u2 | mean daily wind speed **at 2 m above ground** | m/s |\r\n    17\t| Rs | incoming solar radiation, daily total | MJ m-2 day-1 |\r\n    18\t| ea | actual vapour pressure | kPa |\r\n    19\t| J | day of the year: 1 on 1 January, up to 365 (366 in a leap year) | - |\r\n    20\t| latitude | decimal degrees, **north positive, south negative** | deg |\r\n    21\t| z | station elevation above sea level | m |\r\n    22\t\r\n    23\tStation records do not always arrive in this form. Section 3 lists every form our station register and raw files use\r\n    24\tand how each one is converted. The FAO-56 equations themselves (section 2) only ever see the standard form.\r\n    25\t\r\n    26\t## 2. The daily procedure\r\n    27\t\r\n    28\tConstants: solar constant Gsc = 0.0820 MJ m-2 min-1; Stefan-Boltzmann constant sigma = 4.903e-9 MJ K-4 m-2 day-1;\r\n"]
[16.051628, "o", "    29\talbedo of the reference grass 0.23; absolute temperature in Eq. 39 is T + 273.16.\r\n    30\t\r\n    31\t1. Mean temperature (Eq. 9): Tmean = (Tmax + Tmin) / 2.\r\n    32\t2. Air pressure from elevation (Eq. 7): P = 101.3 * ((293 - 0.0065 z) / 293) ^ 5.26, in kPa.\r\n    33\t3. Psychrometric constant (Eq. 8): gamma = 0.665e-3 * P, in kPa/degC.\r\n    34\t4. Saturation vapour pressure at temperature T (Eq. 11): e0(T) = 0.6108 * exp(17.27 T / (T + 237.3)), in kPa.\r\n    35\t5. Mean saturation vapour pressure (Eq. 12): es = (e0(Tmax) + e0(Tmin)) / 2. Do not use e0(Tmean) here.\r\n"]
[16.051651, "o", "    36\t6. Slope of the saturation curve at Tmean (Eq. 13): Delta = 4098 * e0(Tmean) / (Tmean + 237.3)^2, in kPa/degC.\r\n    37\t7. Actual vapour pressure ea, from whichever humidity the station reports (section 3.5):\r\n    38\t   - from daily maximum and minimum relative humidity (Eq. 17): ea = [e0(Tmin) RHmax/100 + e0(Tmax) RHmin/100] / 2;\r\n    39\t   - from the daily mean dewpoint temperature (Eq. 14): ea = e0(Tdew).\r\n    40\t8. Extraterrestrial radiation Ra (Eqs. 21 to 25), with phi = latitude in radians (Eq. 22, negative in the south):\r\n    41\t   - inverse relative Earth-Sun distance (Eq. 23): dr = 1 + 0.033 cos(2 pi J / 365);\r\n    42\t   - solar declination (Eq. 24): delta = 0.409 sin(2 pi J / 365 - 1.39), in radians;\r\n    43\t   - sunset hour angle (Eq. 25): ws = arccos(-tan(phi) tan(delta)), in radians;\r\n"]
[16.051674, "o", "    44\t   - Ra = (24 * 60 / pi) * Gsc * dr * [ws sin(phi) sin(delta) + cos(phi) cos(delta) sin(ws)] (Eq. 21), MJ m-2 day-1.\r\n    45\t   The divisor is 365 in every year, leap years included; J itself runs to 366 in a leap year.\r\n    46\t9. Clear-sky radiation (Eq. 37): Rso = (0.75 + 2e-5 z) * Ra.\r\n    47\t10. Net shortwave radiation (Eq. 38): Rns = (1 - 0.23) * Rs.\r\n"]
[16.051702, "o", "    48\t11. Net longwave radiation (Eq. 39):\r\n    49\t    Rnl = sigma * [(Tmax + 273.16)^4 + (Tmin + 273.16)^4] / 2 * (0.34 - 0.14 sqrt(ea)) * (1.35 Rs/Rso - 0.35),\r\n    50\t    where the ratio Rs/Rso is limited to at most 1.0 before it is used.\r\n    51\t12. Net radiation (Eq. 40): Rn = Rns - Rnl.\r\n    52\t13. Soil heat flux for a daily step (Eq. 42): G = 0.\r\n    53\t14. Reference evapotranspiration (Eq. 6):\r\n    54\t    ET0 = [0.408 Delta (Rn - G) + gamma * 900 / (Tmean + 273) * u2 * (es - ea)] / [Delta + gamma (1 + 0.34 u2)],\r\n    55\t    in mm/day. The factor 0.408 turns MJ m-2 day-1 into mm/day of evaporated water (Eq. 20).\r\n    56\t\r\n    57\t`et0/fao56.py` implements steps 1 to 14, and `python -m et0.selfcheck` checks it against the daily worked example in\r\n    58\tchapter 4 of the book (Example 18, ET0 = 3.88 mm/day).\r\n    59"]
[16.051719, "o", "\t\r\n    60\t## 3. Station register and raw files\r\n    61\t\r\n    62"]
[16.051737, "o", "\t### 3.1 The register (`config/stations.yaml`)\r\n    63\tA YAML file with a list `stations`. Every station has every key below; there are no other forms than the ones listed.\r\n    64\t\r\n    65\t| Key | What it holds |\r\n    66\t|---|---|\r\n    67\t| `id` | station code; the raw file is `<data folder>/<id>.csv` |\r\n"]
[16.051755, "o", "    68\t| `name`, `network` | free text, not used in the calculation |\r\n    69\t| `latitude` | see 3.2 |\r\n    70\t| `longitude` | decimal degrees, east positive; not used by the daily method |\r\n    71\t| `elevation_m` | elevation above sea level in metres (z in Eqs. 7 and 37) |\r\n    72\t| `wind_height_m` | height of the anemometer above ground in metres; see 3.3 |\r\n    73\t| `radiation_units` | unit of the `solar_rad` column; see 3.4 |\r\n    74\t| `humidity` | which humidity columns the raw file has; see 3.5 |\r\n"]
[16.051776, "o", "    75\t\r\n    76\t### 3.2 Latitude\r\n    77\tTwo forms are used:\r\n    78\t- a number: signed decimal degrees, north positive, south negative (`38.42`, `-31.85`);\r\n    79\t- text: unsigned decimal degrees followed directly by the hemisphere letter `N` or `S` (`\"36.95N\"`, `\"34.92S\"`).\r\n    80\t  `\"34.92S\"` is the same place as `-34.92`.\r\n    81\t\r\n    82\t"]
[16.051803, "o", "### 3.3 Wind sensor height\r\n    83\t`wind_ms` is the mean daily wind speed at the anemometer, which may be at any height (any positive value of\r\n    84\t`wind_height_m` between 1 m and 20 m; 2, 3 and 10 m are the most common). The equations need u2, the speed at 2 m.\r\n    85\tConvert with the logarithmic wind profile (Eq. 47), for every station:\r\n    86\t\r\n    87\t    u2 = uz * 4.87 / ln(67.8 z_w - 5.42)\r\n    88\t\r\n    89\twhere uz is the measured speed and z_w the anemometer height in metres. At 10 m the factor is about 0.748; at 2 m it is\r\n"]
[16.051823, "o", "    90\t1.000 (to three decimals).\r\n    91\t\r\n    92\t### 3.4 Radiation units\r\n    93\t- `MJ/m2/day`: daily total incoming solar radiation, already Rs.\r\n    94\t- `W/m2`: daily mean solar irradiance. Multiply by 0.0864 to get Rs in MJ m-2 day-1 (1 W m-2 sustained for a day is\r\n    95\t  86 400 J m-2 = 0.0864 MJ m-2).\r\n    96"]
[16.051841, "o", "\t\r\n    97\t### 3.5 Humidity\r\n    98\t- `rh_minmax`: columns `rh_max_pct` and `rh_min_pct` (daily maximum and minimum relative humidity, %); use Eq. 17.\r\n    99\t- `dewpoint`: column `tdew_c` (daily mean dewpoint temperature, deg C); use Eq. 14.\r\n"]
[16.051866, "o", "   100\t\r\n   101\t### 3.6 Raw daily files (`<data folder>/<id>.csv`)\r\n   102\tOne row per day, no gaps and no missing values. Columns: `date` (YYYY-MM-DD), `tmax_c`, `tmin_c`, the humidity\r\n   103\tcolumn(s) of 3.5, `wind_ms` (m/s at the anemometer height), `solar_rad` (in the station's `radiation_units`).\r\n   104\t\r\n   105\t## 4. Output\r\n   106\tCSV with a header row and the columns `station_id`, `date` (YYYY-MM-DD) and `et0_mm_day`: one row for every station\r\n   107\tand every day in the input. The pipeline writes three decimals.\r\n"]
[16.052106, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[16.052125, "o", "root@98254c38-6d92-484a-af3d-75f7f6376daa:/app# "]
